.TH ADA-QUALITY 1 "2026-11-19" "ada-quality 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ada-quality \- assess and report Ada project quality
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ada-quality
[global options] command [options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Ada Quality registers Ada projects, runs reproducible assessments, persists evidence, and exports text, JSON, SARIF, JUnit, and CSV reports.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B project
Add, discover, synchronize, list, show, enable, disable, relocate, or remove projects.
.TP
.B check, scan
Run a complete assessment or analyze selected changed source files.
.PP
Checks accept --jobs N for bounded parallelism, --reuse-unchanged for exact cache hits, --profile NAME, and
--project-policy. Scans accept --git-diff BASE and combinable --staged, --unstaged, and --untracked modes.
.TP
.B assessment, history, status, regressions, trend
Inspect assessments, aliases, portfolio state, comparisons, and metric history.
.TP
.B report --format json
Export the archive. Use --project, --since, and --until to select a self-contained subset.
.TP
.B report --format html
Write a self-contained portfolio report, optionally with --output FILE.
.TP
.B policy
Initialize, validate, show, discover profiles, or render a project's effective policy.
.TP
.B database
Initialize, check, recover, compact, inspect, back up, export, import, restore, or archive-and-prune the database.
.PP
database archive DEST --before UTC [--keep N] verifies a complete logical archive before removing eligible old
terminal assessments. Running assessments and the newest N terminal assessments per project are retained.
.TP
.B completion bash|zsh|fish
Write a shell completion definition to standard output.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.B --database PATH
Select the database (default .ada-quality.db).
.TP
.B --policy PATH
Select the policy file (default quality-policy.toml).
.TP
.B --format FORMAT, --json
Select machine-readable output where supported.
.TP
.B --output FILE
Write supported reports, findings, scans, trends, and comparisons to a file.
.TP
.B --no-color
Disable terminal styling.
.SH STATUS FILTERS
Use --only unhealthy or --only regressed. Stale filtering requires --only stale together with --since UTC, and selects projects whose latest assessment predates that instant or has no timestamp.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero means success. Assessment or scan violations return 1, usage errors 2, incomplete execution 3, and storage/reporting errors 4.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I quality-policy.toml
Default quality policy.
.TP
.I .ada-quality.db
Default persistent database.
